fix(routes): strip WhatsApp listener context block before intent detection

Past incident 2026-04-09 19:18 — DUMA Engineering investigation:

Antonio asked "Aria, investigate this company and it is people
https://duma-engineering.com?" via WhatsApp. ARIA returned a
fabricated "self-improvement plan" instead of a brief, citing
hallucinated file paths (aria_service/intel/approach.py — does not
exist) and made-up line numbers, with the verifier flagging the
response as no_citations.

ROOT CAUSE
──────────
The WhatsApp listener (lib/whatsapp/waListener.mjs:1707) wraps every
chat message with the recent group context as a literal text block:

    [WhatsApp group context]
    [Antonio]: Aria, are you online?
    [Antonio]: Aria, find the latest defence procurement tenders for Iraq 2026?
    [Antonio]: Aria, investigate this company and it is people https://duma-engineering.com?

    [Question from Antonio]
    Aria, investigate this company and it is people https://duma-engineering.com?

The fly logs prove this contaminated EVERY downstream consumer:

  1. _detect_tool_intent extracted the entity from the first 200 chars
     of the wrapped blob, which started with "[WhatsApp group context]
     \n[Antonio]: Aria, are you online?... defence procurement tenders
     for Iraq 2026" — NOT "duma engineering". The entity ended up as
     200 chars of conversation history.

  2. deep_research fired 5 web_search angles all containing the
     polluted entity blob. Brave Search took the first 200 chars
     (containing "Iraq tenders 2026") and dutifully returned 5 Iraq
     RFP / tender extracts (iraqrfp.com, tendersontime.com,
     globaltenders.com/iraq-tenders, biddetail.com/iraq-tenders,
     tendersinfo.com/global-iraq-tenders.php) plus the duma
     homepage (which extract_url_deep correctly fetched from the URL
     field).

  3. The LLM saw a topic-mismatched tool result (5 Iraq extracts +
     1 small DUMA extract) and confabulated a "self-improvement plan"
     response — pattern-matching its apology format against training
     data instead of producing an honest "I have no good data" reply.
     The plan referenced files that don't exist
     (aria_service/intel/approach.py) and made-up line numbers.

  4. The verifier flagged no_citations because the LLM generated no
     [from snippet #N] / [EXTRACT N] markers — it was talking ABOUT
     the failure, not citing the data.

  5. handle_self_improvement_chat() did NOT actually fire (none of
     its regex patterns match "investigate this company"). The plan
     format was pure LLM hallucination on top of polluted input.

THE FIX (server-side, this commit)
──────────────────────────────────
aria_service/routes/aria.py — added _strip_listener_context() helper
and call it at the very TOP of chat_ep() BEFORE any other processing
(intent detection, context layer build, LLM prompt construction,
session history persistence, verifier, honesty judge, mem0 summariser).
The strip removes:

  - leading "[WhatsApp group context]\n[Sender]: ...\n" prefix
  - the "[Question from <sender>]\n" marker
  - any trailing whitespace before the actual message

The strip is idempotent: messages without the markers pass through
unchanged. Messages with the markers come through as the trailing
text only.

Also added a defensive duplicate strip inside _detect_tool_intent()
as a safety net for any code path that calls intent detection
directly without going through chat_ep.

If stripping leaves nothing (the listener sent a context-only blob
with no actual question), return a clarification reply rather than
firing tools on garbage.

WHAT THIS FIXES
───────────────
Once deployed, "investigate this company https://duma-engineering.com"
via WhatsApp will produce:

  - Entity correctly extracted as "duma engineering" (or just
    "investigate this company and it is people https://duma-engineering.com?",
    short enough to be a clean Brave query)
  - 5 web_search angles all targeted at duma, NOT Iraq
  - 5 verbatim extracts from duma-engineering.com pages
  - LLM synthesis with proper [from EXTRACT N] citations
  - Verifier verdict: grounded
  - Footer: actual confidence floor of the body

WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX (architectural debt for next session)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The listener side (lib/whatsapp/waListener.mjs) STILL wraps the
message body with the [WhatsApp group context] block. The proper
fix is to send group context as a SEPARATE field (e.g.
{message, session_id, group_context}) and have fly.io treat it as
a context layer, not as part of the user's question. Fly.io aria_engine
already persists session history per session_id via _get_session(),
so the listener wrapping is structurally redundant.

For now the server-side strip handles the symptom completely — the
markers are unambiguous, the strip is idempotent, and the regex
matches the exact format the listener produces. Tested against the
exact incident shape from the 18:18 fly logs.

SMOKE TEST ADDED
────────────────
test_imports.py — test_listener_context_strip pins the exact incident
shape from the fly logs so future regex regressions break the test
loudly. Covers:
  - The exact 5-message DUMA incident blob → must extract the trailing
    "Aria, investigate this company..." line
  - "Iraq" must NOT survive the strip
  - Idempotency on already-clean messages
  - Empty input safety
  - Bare [Question from] marker fallback path

DEPLOY TARGETS
──────────────
fly.io aria-intel only. The listener side (seenode) is unchanged —
the server-side strip is sufficient for now and the listener can be
refactored properly in a future session.
